# Code Quality Rules

## No `any` (E1)
`any` is forbidden. Use `unknown` and narrow. Never `// @ts-ignore`. `// @ts-expect-error` only with a justification.

## Prettier + ESLint (E2)
- `npm run format` / `npm run lint` before a PR.
- 2-space indent. Do not add `eslint-disable` without a comment explaining why.

## TypeScript Must Compile Clean (E3)
`npm run build` (`tsc -b`) must pass. Do not cast away errors with `as unknown as X`.

## Tests (E4)
This app has no test runner yet. When tests are added, colocate them (`helper.test.tsx`) and cover new pure logic. Do not add a runner unless the user asks.
